---
import summary from '../../public/generated/media/evidence/toy-summary.json';
import brief from '../../public/generated/media/evidence/toy-brief.json';
import claims from '../../public/generated/media/evidence/toy-claims.json';
import manuscript from '../../../media/evidence/toy-manuscript.md?raw';
const abstract = manuscript.split('## Abstract')[1]?.split('## Question')[0]?.trim();
if (!abstract) throw new Error('The toy report preview needs its original abstract.');
const base = '/allagma/generated/media/evidence/';
const tabs = ['Results', 'Report', 'Claims', 'Brief'];
---
<div class="study-explorer">
  <div class="explorer-label"><span>OFFLINE EXAMPLE / RETAINED OUTPUTS</span><span>toy-v1 · a001</span></div>
  <div class="explorer-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Study artifacts">
    {tabs.map((label, i) => <button type="button" role="tab" id={'tab-'+label.toLowerCase()} aria-controls={'panel-'+label.toLowerCase()} aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1}>{label}</button>)}
  </div>
  <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-results" aria-labelledby="tab-results" tabindex="0">
    <p class="artifact-type">Generated figure and numerical summary</p>
    <h2>Higher average error, with individual counterexamples</h2>
    <p>Each point is one of 24 independent confirmation seeds. Positive differences mean the biased estimator had higher squared error. Three differences are negative and one is zero.</p>
    <figure>
      <a href={base+'toy-paired-differences.svg'} aria-label="Open the full-size toy study figure">
        <img src={base+'toy-paired-differences.svg'} alt="Paired squared-error differences for 24 confirmation seeds. Three seeds have negative differences, one is tied at zero, and the average is positive." width="840" height="640" />
      </a>
      <figcaption>The dashed line marks the mean difference, +{summary.difference.toFixed(5)}. <a href={base+'toy-paired-differences.svg'}>Open the full-size figure</a>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>Approximate 95% interval: [{summary.ci95_normal.map(x => x.toFixed(5)).join(', ')}]. This is the mean ±1.96 standard errors across seeds, not an exact small-sample guarantee.</p>
    <a class="artifact-source" href={base+'toy-summary.json'}>Read the exact numerical summary →</a>
  </section>
  <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-report" aria-labelledby="tab-report" tabindex="0" hidden>
    <p class="artifact-type">Generated manuscript / abstract excerpt</p>
    <h2>A reproducible comparison of two mean estimators</h2>
    <blockquote>{abstract}</blockquote>
    <h3>Results reported in the manuscript</h3>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Recomputed quantity</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sample-mean MSE</td><td>{summary.mean_mse.toFixed(8)}</td></tr><tr><td>Biased-estimator MSE</td><td>{summary.biased_mse.toFixed(8)}</td></tr><tr><td>Paired difference</td><td>{summary.difference.toFixed(8)}</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <p>The full manuscript explains the question, mathematical expectation, methods, findings and limitations. Its claim ledger points to the measurements behind each statement.</p>
    <a class="artifact-source" href={base+'toy-manuscript.md'} download="toy-manuscript.md">Download the full generated manuscript (Markdown) →</a>
    <p class="explorer-boundary">Relative references inside that file resolve in the full study. <a href="/allagma/guides/first-study/">Run the tutorial</a> to generate it and recompute the report.</p>
  </section>
  <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-claims" aria-labelledby="tab-claims" tabindex="0" hidden>
    <p class="artifact-type">Generated claim ledger</p>
    <h2>Which statements do the results support?</h2>
    <p>The average comparison and the claim about every seed have different answers. Each entry keeps its scope and supporting or contradicting evidence.</p>
    {claims.map(claim => <article class="explorer-claim"><div><span class="artifact-type">{claim.claim_id}</span><span class:list={['claim-state', claim.status]}>{claim.status}</span></div><p>{claim.text}</p><details><summary>Evidence scope and references</summary><p>{claim.scope}</p><ul>{claim.limitations.map(x => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Evidence reference JSON">{JSON.stringify({ supporting: claim.supporting, contradicting: claim.contradicting }, null, 2)}</pre></details></article>)}
    <a class="artifact-source" href={base+'toy-claims.json'}>Read the exact claim ledger →</a>
  </section>
  <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-brief" aria-labelledby="tab-brief" tabindex="0" hidden>
    <p class="artifact-type">Original study brief</p>
    <h2>{brief.question}</h2>
    <p>The example has a known mathematical answer. That makes it useful for learning how to plan a study, run it and check the resulting report.</p>
    <h3>Completion criteria from the brief</h3>
    <ul>{brief.success_criteria.map(x => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
    <p class="explorer-boundary">The introductory example supplies its scientific code. In a <a href="/allagma/guides/native-study/">native study</a>, the agent develops that code from your question and materials.</p>
    <a class="artifact-source" href={base+'toy-brief.json'}>Read the exact brief JSON →</a>
  </section>
  <div class="explorer-footer"><span>Selected files from the offline example.</span><a href={base+'provenance.json'}>Artifact sources and digests →</a></div>
</div>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.study-explorer').forEach(explorer => {
    const tabs = Array.from(explorer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]'));
    function select(tab: HTMLButtonElement, updateHash = true) {
      for (const candidate of tabs) {
        const selected = candidate === tab;
        candidate.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
        candidate.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1;
        const panel = explorer.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#'+candidate.getAttribute('aria-controls'));
        if (panel) panel.hidden = !selected;
      }
      if (updateHash) history.replaceState(null, '', '#'+tab.getAttribute('aria-controls'));
    }
    function selectFromHash() {
      const target = tabs.find(tab => '#'+tab.getAttribute('aria-controls') === location.hash || '#'+tab.id === location.hash);
      if (target) select(target, false);
    }
    selectFromHash();
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', selectFromHash);
    for (const tab of tabs) {
      tab.addEventListener('click', () => select(tab));
      tab.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
        const index = tabs.indexOf(tab);
        let next;
        if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') next = tabs[(index + 1) % tabs.length];
        if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') next = tabs[(index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
        if (event.key === 'Home') next = tabs[0];
        if (event.key === 'End') next = tabs[tabs.length - 1];
        if (next) { event.preventDefault(); select(next); next.focus(); }
      });
    }
  });
</script>
<style>
  .study-explorer { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--panel); overflow: hidden; }
  .explorer-label, .explorer-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; font: .72rem/1.5 var(--sl-font-mono); color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; }
  .explorer-tabs { display: flex; gap: .5rem; padding: 0 1.2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; }
  .explorer-tabs button { background: transparent; border: 0; border-bottom: 3px solid transparent; color: var(--muted); cursor: pointer; padding: .85rem .7rem; font: inherit; font-size: .95rem; margin: 0; }
  .explorer-tabs button[aria-selected='true'] { color: var(--teal); border-bottom-color: var(--teal); font-weight: 650; }
  [role='tabpanel'] { padding: 1.5rem; margin: 0; }[hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .artifact-type { font: .75rem/1.5 var(--sl-font-mono); color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 .8rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: .5rem 0 1.1rem; }h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  p, li { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; }.explorer-boundary { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  .artifact-source { display: inline-block; font-size: .95rem; margin-top: .8rem; color: var(--teal); }
  figure { margin: 1.2rem 0; }img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  figcaption { font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .8rem; }
  blockquote { padding: .25rem 0 .25rem 1.2rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.8rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .explorer-claim { padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }.explorer-claim > div { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; }.explorer-claim .artifact-type { margin: 0; }.explorer-claim p { margin: .8rem 0; }
  details { font-size: .9rem; }summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--teal); }pre { overflow: auto; max-height: 20rem; padding: 1rem; background: var(--paper); font-size: .75rem; }
  .explorer-footer { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); flex-wrap: wrap; }.explorer-footer a { color: var(--teal); }
  @media (max-width: 500px) { .explorer-label { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem; padding: 1rem; }[role='tabpanel'] { padding: 1rem; }h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; }.explorer-tabs { padding-inline: .4rem; gap: .2rem; }.explorer-tabs button { font-size: .9rem; padding-inline: .6rem; } }
</style>
